; Reject the phrase
;
; Called (or jumped to) when the words do not fit the grammar. While an order
; after SAY TO is being parsed (#R$75F1 gives NZ) the error is ignored and the
; routine just returns. For the player's own line it discards one return
; address and falls into #R$7929, which prints "What ?" and returns NZ to the
; caller's caller, so parsing stops.
;
; O:F NZ (order text: returns to the caller)
@label=RejectPhrase
c$7924 CALL $75F1    ;
 $7927 RET NZ        ; an order: ignore the error
 $7928 POP HL        ; drop the caller: end the parse
